{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies","id":1273660,"title":"Drowned Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-09T21:25:57-08:00","id":1273660,"title":"Drowned Legacies","content":"The Drowned Legacies are the half-cryptid vampires rumored to have once inhabited South America. Similar to the Laibon of Africa, they are believed by some to be bloodlines or variants, while others see in them a phenomenon similar to the Kuei-jin of East Asia. They are featured in BJD. <br /> <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on the Drowned Legacies?<br /> <br /> <br /> Why not have some of them appear in Central America and North America?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T21:52:03-08:00","id":1273664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies#post1273660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Drowned Legacies are the half-cryptid vampires rumored to have once inhabited South America. Similar to the Laibon of Africa, they are believed by some to be bloodlines or variants, while others see in them a phenomenon similar to the Kuei-jin of East Asia. They are featured in BJD.<br /> <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on the Drowned Legacies?<br /> <br /> <br /> Why not have some of them appear in Central America and North America?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They are in CBN</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:08:09-08:00","id":1273676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273664#post1273664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They are in CBN</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what that means/stands for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T01:34:01-08:00","id":1273687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273676#post1273676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what that means/stands for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago by Night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T02:32:10-08:00","id":1273690,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see how the Drowned Legacies turn out - the Example in CbN is very interesting, but in fairness is quite open to interpretation right now - most likely as there aren't rules or a core book for them and as such they can't give masses of detail.<br /> <br /> i don't know if i want them to be similar to the Laibon, with a direct if occluded connection to the Clans, or the KotE and a whole new breed of Beasties. One thing is for sure, there is enough similarity for them to pass as Kindred if the CbN example is anything to go by.<br /> <br /> One thing i quite like is how we're starting to see Vampire races somehow align against the various Wraith Kingdoms. In the same way that you need a different style of Necromancy to control Wraiths from different parts of the 'world', it seems the differences in Soul matter spit out different forms of Blood sucker! In the Abrahamic regions (Kingdom of Iron) where there is one, all powerful God/Creator, we've got Caine - a singular (with the second generation somewhat acting as the Holy trinity), all powerful Creator. In the Asian territories (Kingdom of Jade) where there is more focus on Karma, Dhama, Rebirth and a Pantheon of Gods, we've got Self creating Vampires with a closer connection to the spirit world, but also a greater divide in their souls (Hun and Po). With the Laibon (Kingdom of Ivory), it feels like Western Religion has influenced and encroached on it, but local customs have reshaped it into something unique with again, a greater focus on Duality and the parts of the soul - but more in harmony that the KotE - it makes for an interesting dynamic as well as a critique on Colonialism.Interestingly if this is the case, then the Ministry/Setites could be onto something by saying that Set isn't a Cainite, as he could be the Vampire from the Kingdom of Sand - somehow kept all that potential for himself, but also merged it with the more mainstream Cainites. Saulot is also an interesting example of what happens when one type of vampire tries to emulate the soul makeup of another - we get his split soul and the creation of his many bloodlines...<br /> <br /> i'm hopeful that the Drowned legacy takes on the perspective of the Kingdom of Obsidian and whatever form that might take. it could again take elements of Cainite blood due to Western Colonialism, but perhaps due to the lakes of blood spilled by the ancient cultures, it has diluted to the point where they're unrecognizable and similar to thin bloods, but with time and spiritual power the blood has thickened back up again to make them something totally different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","user":"chipotlechris","date":". 12-10-2018, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T03:30:58-08:00","id":1273696,"title":"","content":"I thought time ago in a &quot;Kindred of the Esmerald Kingdom&quot; with diverse variations of the clans of the Old World. The Gangrel, Nosferatu and Tlacique would be the principal bloodlines in the precolombine cultures, and I though in a bloodline Brujah created by Menele in the Inca Empire.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm awaiting more information. I hope there's not bizarre bloodlines, and a cultural adaptation of the american vampires similar to the Old World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:47:12-08:00","id":1273716,"title":"","content":"In my head-canon and in things I am using for my game, the Drowned Legacies are a mix. I have the Tlacique as a full populated legacy, and there are some others that will have a decent population base, but there are others that are singular, or of a singular embrace lineage. One of the characters in my Tucson game is descended along one such lineage, and he doesn't even know that. As far as he and the rest of the world are concerned, he is a Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T20:15:42-08:00","id":1273833,"title":"","content":"Here is some research about the names used for the six known Drowned Legacies;<br /> <br /> Cipactli; 'Crocodile' was the first day of the Aztec divinatory count of 13 X 20 days. So, Nahuatl vampires in Mexico.<br /> <br /> Karai Pyrahe; I can\u2019t find any etymological origins for the word. But Google search suggested Karai Perak (which is a town in Malaysia), and Kare Praha (which is apparently a heavy equipment company near Prague).<br /> <br /> Kalku; Kalku in Mapuche (Mapuches are a group of indigenous inhabitants of south-central Chile and southwestern Argentina, including parts of present-day Patagonia.) mythology, is a sorcerer or witch who works with black magic and negative powers or forces. So, Mapuche vampires in Chile, and Argentina.<br /> <br /> Lostundo; I can\u2019t find any etymological origins for the word.<br /> <br /> Titlacauan; Another Aztec diety, one associated with a wide range of concepts, including the night sky, the night winds, hurricanes, the north, the earth, obsidian, enmity, discord, rulership, divination, temptation, jaguars, sorcery, beauty, war and strife. So, another group of Nahuatl vampires in Mexico.<br /> <br /> Unhudo; According to folklore, the Unhudo is a kind of undead with clothes in bad condition, who has big nails and wears a straw hat. Their goal is to haunt anyone who dares steal fruit, flowers or do any harm to the forest. These legends come from S\u00e3o Paulo, Brazil. So, Brazilian vampires who are possibly connected to the native Tupi people.<br /> <br /> So, where do the terms \u201cLostundo\u201d and \u201cKarai Pyrahe\u201d come from?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T21:05:31-08:00","id":1273839,"title":"","content":"Los Tundo I think can mean the Prickers, which could fit with some ritual magic as many Nuhuallotl Magic\u2019s involve shedding blood through pricking with a cactus needle. It can also mean I think the turners or the shearers, but I would go with the Prickers, or let\u2019s shorten that to the pricks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T03:12:58-08:00","id":1273858,"title":"","content":"Karai Pyhare is in guaran\u00ed, a language spoken in Paraguay, where I'm from. It should actually be written as Kara'\u00ed Pyhare, with accent on the last syllable in both words. Kara'\u00ed means mr. or lord, and pyhare means nighttime. So together it means lord of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T03:28:45-08:00","id":1273859,"title":"","content":"The research into the names is interesting, and whilst i'm sure it isn't even anything remotely like this, it's fun to speculate and we're all geeks here! so with that in mind - potential bloodlines based on this?<br /> <br /> Cipactli; 'Crocodile' was the first day of the Aztec divinatory count of 13 X 20 days. So, Nahuatl vampires in Mexico.<br /> *So, with a reptile association could be a Setite Relation? although we've already got the Tlalique so not sure we need another<br /> <br /> Karai Pyhare is in guaran\u00ed, a language spoken in Paraguay, where I'm from. It should actually be written as Kara'\u00ed Pyhare, with accent on the last syllable in both words. Kara'\u00ed means mr. or lord, and pyhare means nighttime. So together it means lord of the night.<br /> *Lords of the Night? Sounds like a shoe in for the Lasombra, but also Ventrue could work and lord knows we don't see many bloodlines come out from them.<br /> <br /> Kalku; Kalku in Mapuche (Mapuches are a group of indigenous inhabitants of south-central Chile and southwestern Argentina, including parts of present-day Patagonia.) mythology, is a sorcerer or witch who works with black magic and negative powers or forces. So, Mapuche vampires in Chile, and Argentina.<br /> *Sorceror? Well, that'll be the Banu Haqim then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Los Tundo I think can mean the Prickers, which could fit with some ritual magic as many Nuhuallotl Magic\u2019s involve shedding blood through pricking with a cactus needle<br /> *Not sure on this one. so many Clans fit the definition of Pricks! too much choice, but at least we can exclude the Tremere who would otherwise be the obvious choice due to their age <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Titlacauan; Another Aztec diety, one associated with a wide range of concepts, including the night sky, the night winds, hurricanes, the north, the earth, obsidian, enmity, discord, rulership, divination, temptation, jaguars, sorcery, beauty, war and strife. So, another group of Nahuatl vampires in Mexico.*<br /> *Something here makes me feel Tzimisce, perhaps the natural connection, but perhaps the word 'Strife'<br /> <br /> Unhudo; According to folklore, the Unhudo is a kind of undead with clothes in bad condition, who has big nails and wears a straw hat. Their goal is to haunt anyone who dares steal fruit, flowers or do any harm to the forest. These legends come from S\u00e3o Paulo, Brazil. So, Brazilian vampires who are possibly connected to the native Tupi people.<br /> *Well, we know the Toreador love flowers and i can see how a certain number or them could rock the right hat and nails combo! However, i'm leaning Gangrel for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T03:32:57-08:00","id":1273860,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying this discussion. To confirm: the names weren't chosen at random, and experts on history and mythology from Central and South America were consulted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T03:51:28-08:00","id":1273863,"title":"","content":"If I remember my folklore correctly, Karai pyhare is a name for the pombero, a small, impish hairy man that could do everything the legacy can. And yes, a common practice for out-of-wedlock pregnancies was claiming he did it.<br /> He also loved alcohol and cigars, so basically a hairier baron samedi. I'd personally peg them as gangrel, nos or maybe ravnos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T05:40:27-08:00","id":1273872,"title":"","content":"I just want some pishtacos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T07:02:38-08:00","id":1273882,"title":"","content":"I think the Drowned Legacies are more interesting when they have no easy connection to the known clans. So making the Cipactli just a Settite bloodline would be dull. But I can see using the known disciplines for the sake of mechanical simplicity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273858#post1273858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Karai Pyhare is in guaran\u00ed, a language spoken in Paraguay, where I'm from. It should actually be written as Kara'\u00ed Pyhare, with accent on the last syllable in both words. Kara'\u00ed means mr. or lord, and pyhare means nighttime. So together it means lord of the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. That for posting this message.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T07:58:42-08:00","id":1273889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273882#post1273882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Drowned Legacies are more interesting when they have no easy connection to the known clans. So making the Cipactli just a Settite bloodline would be dull. But I can see using the known disciplines for the sake of mechanical simplicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Agree, but unless they're totally different species than the KotE, then this is always a possibility and something that people will always be looking for. And to be fair to myself, i did say i didn't think it was anything as simple as that. It was worth it to make the Toreador/Hat/Nails remark. <br /> <br /> Having re-read Nerissa in CbN today, we know they'll use classic disciplines (or at least things that are similar enough to use those names as a holding place for now), and knowing what we know about the flexible nature of Disciplines in V5 (Protean/Serpentis/Vicissitude have merged for example), just the Headline names only gives us an indication of the types of powers they have.<br /> <br /> We've had a totally separate species of Vampire (KotE), and also variations on the main clans where they diverged a significant period of time ago (The African Legacies). A possible theory is they'll be something in a similar vein to cainites, but even further removed than the legacies, perhaps something that predates the antediluvians. Now, could it be the second generation survived in some way, or other antediluvians apart from the classic 13 that escaped in the flood and made a new base (Calling themselves drowned certainly has some interesting connotations when we consider the biblical deluge). Could it predate even them? Nerissa is a Lilith cultist, perhaps the drowned legacies don't have a Dark Father in Caine, perhaps their ultimate progenitor was Lilith? she taught caine and there are so many conflicting stories about her, she could just as easily share what amounts to the same curse. If this is the case, then we'd have a species that share common DNA to Cainites, but branched out much further up the tree - Lillian Marsupials to Cainite Mammals as a more real world example.<br /> <br /> Will we ever know for sure? whilst i look forward to knowing more detail, part of the fun is the speculation. As long as their is a definitive answer (even if it's open to interpretation) that is hinted at then i'm happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T09:03:24-08:00","id":1273897,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m always a fan of some uncertainty in a Legacy/Clan/Bloodlines origins. And I like the idea that maybe the Laibon or the Drowned are of Liliths kith, as some of the books mentioned Lilith May have had some of her children take their place among the Antes.<br /> <br /> And I like the idea of uncertain apocryphal links hinting maybe at more then one clan for mysteries sake. Like Analects of the 3rd Garden has Ilyes the Brujah Progenitor display hints of being the first to develop Necromancy (from his scholarly ways) and a 3rd eye (a gift from his sister Malkav painted on his head as he journeys east).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T09:06:54-08:00","id":1273898,"title":"","content":"And I loved the idea of Zapathsura having origins created by the gods to scourge the thousand demons. But I was disappointed when they ignored that and had the Sword of Night tie them to Cainite myth in Lore of Clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T09:34:40-08:00","id":1273900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chipotlechris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273889#post1273889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nerissa is a Lilith cultist, perhaps the drowned legacies don't have a Dark Father in Caine, perhaps their ultimate progenitor was Lilith?</div> </div> </div> </div>That still ties it too much to the standard Judeo-Christian stories, in as much as Lilith is a product of Jewish folklore. Native American vampires should be there own thing, or as much their own thing as possible.<br /> <br /> If I had to nail it down, I would suggest they were a kind of tulpa. Enough people believed in blood-drinking, night-time bogey men and night-time, blood-drining bogey men appeared. They have no connection to Caine, even if some of them choose to worship Lilith. Or at least some manifestation of Lilith. The standard disciplines, and some kind of banes, are used for the sake of mechanical simplicity. (One of the problems with KotE is the mechanical complexity). But otherwise, the DLs are their own species.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T10:07:34-08:00","id":1273904,"title":"","content":"I think though Lilith can work rather well even divorced from Judeochristian as you can essentially reveal a similar scorned goddess figure is tied to Lilith, and it\u2019s just Cainites who bring the Lilith Baggage. Kindred of the East did this by having the Scarlet Empress figure, vampires of Europe know her as Lilith but to the Wan Gui they know of a vague and primal force of Yang, oddly enough also a force of femininity. She was a minister of Creation.<br /> <br /> You can play with expectations this way. You may call her Lilith it we know her as the scorned mother of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T11:15:39-08:00","id":1273913,"title":"","content":"What I'm curious about is how much they have in common with each other. They all seem to be wildly different from one another, apart from basic vampire things they share with any other vampiric creature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T13:08:47-08:00","id":1273939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273913#post1273913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm curious about is how much they have in common with each other. They all seem to be wildly different from one another, apart from basic vampire things they share with any other vampiric creature</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that like the Laibon these Legacies might appear more like spirits or Demons the. Specifically just blood drinking corpses. So instead of just heart Beatless humans they may seem like monstrous demonic or other depending on the character. Like things like animal features or strange effects like burning eyes or haloes or rotting plants with their touch are a thing. Something to really separate them from humanity if they drift in an inhuman direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T03:16:34-08:00","id":1274008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273900#post1273900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still ties it too much to the standard Judeo-Christian stories, in as much as Lilith is a product of Jewish folklore. Native American vampires should be there own thing, or as much their own thing as possible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, and i think that's the right approach, but it as said above it could still be that what 'we' call Lilith, they call something else. I personally hope it's similar in some way to my first thought - it's that version of the Underworlds way of answering the same problem - Asia has KotE, Europe and middle east has Cainites, Africa has Laibon and America has the Drowned. At some point in the distant past, Someone refused to 'die' and they became the first and have passed down their curse. We've tied it into Bible stories, but it represents far more primal forces of nature and creation. The fact that they have similar mechanics isn't an issue and still makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T10:00:47-08:00","id":1274064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chipotlechris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273889#post1273889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had a totally separate species of Vampire (KotE), and also variations on the main clans where they diverged a significant period of time ago (The African Legacies). A possible theory is they'll be something in a similar vein to cainites, but even further removed than the legacies, perhaps something that predates the antediluvians. Now, could it be the second generation survived in some way, or other antediluvians apart from the classic 13 that escaped in the flood and made a new base (Calling themselves drowned certainly has some interesting connotations when we consider the biblical deluge). Could it predate even them? Nerissa is a Lilith cultist, perhaps the drowned legacies don't have a Dark Father in Caine, perhaps their ultimate progenitor was Lilith? she taught caine and there are so many conflicting stories about her, she could just as easily share what amounts to the same curse. If this is the case, then we'd have a species that share common DNA to Cainites, but branched out much further up the tree - Lillian Marsupials to Cainite Mammals as a more real world example.<br /> <br /> Will we ever know for sure? whilst i look forward to knowing more detail, part of the fun is the speculation. As long as their is a definitive answer (even if it's open to interpretation) that is hinted at then i'm happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>regarding the Second Generation, I have my pet-theory<br /> here and there is mentioned a fourth 2nd Generation guy, Dracian (ok, there're The Hag and the King and Queen of Enoch, but we don't talk about them)<br /> said Dracian was apparently the Sire of both Gangrel and Ravnos Antedeluvians and was offed (much more time before the fall of the 2nd city) by the Gangrel Ante with the old trick of &quot;stake and sunlight&quot; which resulted in the Gangrel and Ravnos archetypical hate for each other.<br /> Now, this story is told by the Ravnos, which for their &quot;peculiarities&quot; could maybe be seen as interlocutor even less reliable than the norm.<br /> So what we know is that this &quot;Dracian&quot; is:<br /> -the Sire of Gangrel and Ravnos, which both share in some manner a sort of wanderlust<br /> -was not around anymore by the time the 2nd Generation got their little surprise in the 2nd City<br /> <br /> So, we can assume Dracian was a traveler and he may have just &quot;disappeared&quot; from the 2nd city for some reasons (chiefly because his brethren were boring).<br /> Also this would mean that the Ravnos Ante scammed the Gangrel one, forcing on her the supposed death of their Sire, but let's not go there...<br /> <br /> So, what if Dracian wandered in the american massland on the footsteps of the prehistorical migrant populations, and just created his own progeny?<br /> we would have a total different breed of vampires that if even are Cainites, are totally unrelated to the Kindred.<br /> Also several instances of the WoD point at the fact that the form follows the thought. This means that supernatural beings of the same genesis aren't necessarily going to follow the same path. A breed of &quot;Antediluvians&quot; in a totally different environment can probably evolve in a whole different way than the Old World ones.<br /> ...<br /> and nonetheless they respect some of the Cainites rules, like Generation, so that western vampires could Diablerize them back in the colonization era and safely assume they were strains and offshots of the main Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":24483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","user":"SalamanDer","date":". 12-12-2018, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T10:40:25-08:00","id":1274072,"title":"","content":"by the way, a rightful objection to my theory is that I'm the only one still remembering the old Dracian, so chance are their actual roots are totally different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T21:15:40-08:00","id":1274134,"title":"","content":"Some kind of Drowned Legacy appears in the manuscript for Chicago by Night 5th. Actually, there might be more than one type of Legacy present - the text is vague. In any case, what do you suppose it is, assuming it is a single Legacy? I am inclined to say either a baykok or a mishipeshu.<br /> <br /> <i>Baykok</i>: It is said to fly through the forests of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">Great Lakes</a> region. The cries of Baykok are also described as being shrill. Described as &quot;Death&quot; in <i>The Song of Hiawatha</i>, it is said to appear as an extremely emaciated skeleton-like figure, with thin translucent skin and glowing red points for eyes.<br /> <br /> <i>Mishipeshu</i>: To the Algonquins, the underwater panther (mishipeshu) was the most powerful underworld being. It has the head and paws of a giant cat but is covered in scales and has dagger-like spikes running along its back and tail.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the bayok, which were also called the pakak. But it could be the mishipeshu, given the tendancy to sleep at the bottom of Lake Michigan. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T21:31:08-08:00","id":1274135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1273882#post1273882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Drowned Legacies are more interesting when they have no easy connection to the known clans. So making the Cipactli just a Settite bloodline would be dull. But I can see using the known disciplines for the sake of mechanical simplicity.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is one advantage to V5 and its consolidation of disciplines people can't go &quot;Oh it has serpentis its just Followers of set in a funny hat&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T03:55:09-08:00","id":1274167,"title":"","content":"Having read over the Drowned Legacy description on the Wikia, i'm not inclined to say that Nerissa fits in with any in particular, and the <i>Baykok </i>and<i> Mishipshu</i> you mention above, i've not heard of before, but nothing in the physical description sounds like Nerissa. She also has no Protean or powers associated with Death. However the <i>Mishepshu</i> seems an interesting fit because of the '<i>underwater panther' </i>comment. Also, the Algonquin were Canadian Natives (according to t'internet) which adjoins the Great lakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24788-chipotlechris","name":"chipotlechris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24788_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T06:15:19-08:00","id":1274182,"title":"","content":"Its possible that Caine is just a lot older than we thought. I mean the First and Second cities were hard to place in a timeline but some are saying no older than 10,000. We have found baby remains as old as 11,000 in the americas. So maybe Caine is just the name we know him as but he is far older than that. Maybe thats just a name we know him as but was never his true name. Perhaps like the Tremere or Nagaraja he was an ancient mage and vamped himself. Maybe he was cursed by god, or a demon with vampiric powers.<br /> <br /> The Drowned Legacies could easily be a sibling set to our Kindred whos origin just never got recorded, if they followed the mortals into the new landmasses maybe they where all thought to have met final death by the time the Ante's were sired, or just forgotten about by everyone who wrote them off so long ago there is noone active with a living memory of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10872-thelastsane1","name":"TheLastSane1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T10:00:51-08:00","id":1274212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274134#post1274134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some kind of Drowned Legacy appears in the manuscript for Chicago by Night 5th. Actually, there might be more than one type of Legacy present - the text is vague. In any case, what do you suppose it is, assuming it is a single Legacy? I am inclined to say either a baykok or a mishipeshu.<br /> <br /> <i>Baykok</i>: It is said to fly through the forests of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">Great Lakes</a> region. The cries of Baykok are also described as being shrill. Described as &quot;Death&quot; in <i>The Song of Hiawatha</i>, it is said to appear as an extremely emaciated skeleton-like figure, with thin translucent skin and glowing red points for eyes.<br /> <br /> <i>Mishipeshu</i>: To the Algonquins, the underwater panther (mishipeshu) was the most powerful underworld being. It has the head and paws of a giant cat but is covered in scales and has dagger-like spikes running along its back and tail.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the bayok, which were also called the pakak. But it could be the mishipeshu, given the tendancy to sleep at the bottom of Lake Michigan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got late to join the Chicago wagon (RL's been kind of taxing lately), Baykok and Mishipeshu are the actual names used?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T13:53:17-08:00","id":1274244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheLastSane1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274182#post1274182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its possible that Caine is just a lot older than we thought. I mean the First and Second cities were hard to place in a timeline but some are saying no older than 10,000. We have found baby remains as old as 11,000 in the americas. So maybe Caine is just the name we know him as but he is far older than that. Maybe thats just a name we know him as but was never his true name. Perhaps like the Tremere or Nagaraja he was an ancient mage and vamped himself. Maybe he was cursed by god, or a demon with vampiric powers.<br /> <br /> The Drowned Legacies could easily be a sibling set to our Kindred whos origin just never got recorded, if they followed the mortals into the new landmasses maybe they where all thought to have met final death by the time the Ante's were sired, or just forgotten about by everyone who wrote them off so long ago there is noone active with a living memory of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then we basically have to throw out everything &quot;Caine&quot; like. Unless we are going to go with an idea that 1000 BCE jews had some vampire explain prehistory to them. I mean the baby remains are special because they are DNA of a completely lost lineage, we've found remains up to 15k years old and some estimates based on genetic mapping may have had the pre New world ancestors cut off from the rest of the human population 36k Years ago.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T14:40:02-08:00","id":1274251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chipotlechris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274167#post1274167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read over the Drowned Legacy description on the Wikia, i'm not inclined to say that Nerissa fits in with any in particular, and the <i>Baykok </i>and<i> Mishipshu</i> you mention above, i've not heard of before, but nothing in the physical description sounds like Nerissa. She also has no Protean or powers associated with Death. However the <i>Mishepshu</i> seems an interesting fit because of the '<i>underwater panther' </i>comment. Also, the Algonquin were Canadian Natives (according to t'internet) which adjoins the Great lakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of how they look, well, maybe they can control or disguise that - I doubt the Cipactli always looked like crocodiles or someone would have noticed. Also, there maybe be more than one Legacy is Chicago, with Nerissa being one and the creatures buried under the Mason building another. Perhaps she is Mishipshu, and they are Baykok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274212#post1274212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got late to join the Chicago wagon (RL's been kind of taxing lately), Baykok and Mishipeshu are the actual names used?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am just speculating. The Drowned Legacies of South America are named after the real-world legends and folklore of Native Americans. So, I was looking for a suitable name for a Drowned Legacy near Chicago. That brought me to the legends of the Algonquin.<br /> <br /> This is all just fan speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T15:25:09-08:00","id":1274259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274251#post1274251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I am just speculating. The Drowned Legacies of South America are named after the real-world legends and folklore of Native Americans. So, I was looking for a suitable name for a Drowned Legacy near Chicago. That brought me to the legends of the Algonquin.<br /> <br /> This is all just fan speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood<br /> I did got a bit overexcited for some reasons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thank you for your time :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:38:28-07:00","id":1397436,"title":"","content":"<i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In honor of the Cult of the Blood Gods and the Hecata: &quot;Thread Necromancy!&quot; </span></span></span></div></i><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;The angels left God and pursued Lilith, whom they overtook in the midst of the sea, in the mighty waters wherein the Egyptians were destined to drown. They told her God's word, but she did not wish to return. The angels said, &quot;We shall drown you in the sea.&quot; </i>Nicely appropriated, taken in a different context Genesis thingy to justify &quot;The Drowned&quot; as bloodlines descended from Lilith, the &quot;mother of monsters&quot;. The<i> Mishipeshu</i> becomes a distinct bloodline, the &quot;underwater panther&quot;- I translate that as a shapeshifter, a vampire with Protean, with a unique Protean power to change into something terrible- no different than the Tzimisce with their Zulo form, and the Meshipeshu's form is suitably amphibious. If you're hell bent on a Cainite origin, it becomes a specific Gangrel bloodline. For another bloodline, I prefer '<i>Pakak</i>' to Baykok; which is a different word for the same thing. I imagine this bloodline of Lilith is much like the Nosferatu, not a pretty creature to behold; gaunt and skeletal- very much like the Cappadocians (Harbingers of Skulls), with a Bane like the Nagaraja- consuming blood rich organs such as the liver. Nerissa becomes a third bloodline of Lilith, the first of her bloodlines? Western Noddists might name them the &quot;<i>Lilu</i>&quot; or &quot;<i>Lilitu</i>&quot;.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T16:50:38-07:00","id":1398083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274135#post1274135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is one advantage to V5 and its consolidation of disciplines people can't go &quot;Oh it has serpentis its just Followers of set in a funny hat&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, now it's oh they are just &quot;Gangrel who are way into Egyptian/Native religion.&quot; Which is so much better!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T21:03:51-07:00","id":1398116,"title":"","content":"I have a very weird desire and that's for DIABLERIE: MEXICO to become way more important than it was originally. I've always liked Mictlantecuhtli and I think that no one would mind it terribly if it was canonized that &quot;officially&quot; Mictlantecuhtli killed the shit out of the diablerists who invaded his tomb and has since risen from torpor to become a major player in the region. He could be our 2nd Drowned Legacy NPC (or technically our first) who has been organizing the take-back of Mexico from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> He could be an Ur-Shulgi figure or he might have a very different view of Christianity than his Banu Haqim opposite number.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mictlantecuhtli is a polytheist and does not have issues with his subjects worshiping the Christian God, he slept through most of the suffering at the foreign god's worshiper's hands, but he does expect to be venerated as a god as well. You are expected to make blood offerings and shows of fealty to him in addition to whatever other deity or saint you venerate. Some Christians and nonbelievers have no issue with this while others simmer with rage at the perceived blasphemy of it all.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chipotlechris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1274008#post1274008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, and i think that's the right approach, but it as said above it could still be that what 'we' call Lilith, they call something else. I personally hope it's similar in some way to my first thought - it's that version of the Underworlds way of answering the same problem - Asia has KotE, Europe and middle east has Cainites, Africa has Laibon and America has the Drowned. At some point in the distant past, Someone refused to 'die' and they became the first and have passed down their curse. We've tied it into Bible stories, but it represents far more primal forces of nature and creation. The fact that they have similar mechanics isn't an issue and still makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Lilith worship works well for them but have some thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. They should be descendants of Antediluvians who left the First City before the Deluge and thus were never part of the 13 Vampire Clans that formed the Second City under Ventrue (Or Ventrue/Lasombra/Haqim)<br /> <br /> 2. They should have their own origin story wholly divorced from Judeo Christian mythology.<br /> <br /> 3. It might be interesting if the Drowned actually have dozens of competing creator myths and don't actually pay it as much attention as Cainites. &quot;The Olmecs believe... the Mayans believe...the Incans believe...&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. I actually think some Drowned SHOULD be Caine believers because one thing that made Kuei-Jin somewhat &quot;off&quot; is it ignored modern developments of the fact there's a billion Muslims living in Asia. There should be Central American and South American believers in the Christian version of vampirism because it is their mortal belief structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-22-2020, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T21:27:46-07:00","id":1398120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273660-drowned-legacies?p=1398116#post1398116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. I actually think some Drowned SHOULD be Caine believers because one thing that made Kuei-Jin somewhat 